  {
   "id": "MGEmrtJ-AQAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2020-04-09T12:39:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: Creating object of class lavaan from estimated parameters",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\">I calculated model parameters based on, say, 1000 simulations</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>What do you mean &quot;calculated model parameters&quot;?  Did you use MCMC estimation, like is implemented in the blavaan package?</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\">I would like to use the average of the results to generate an object of class lavaan. Using this output I would like to be able to runs methods like summary, lavInspect, predict, etc. <br></div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><br>Is this possible?</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div> It depends what you mean by &quot;results&quot; and what you want to retrieve from the manufactured lavaan object.  If all you have are point estimates, you could hypothetically use lavaan&#39;s internals to easily obtain things like the model-implied moments or the correlation residuals.  But your &quot;results&quot; would also need estimates of uncertainty if you wanted to obtain test statistics.</div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422163845000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2erugpmsI3RjBc3lIVwvP4\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div><div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
